A '''player-owned house''' (often shortened to '''POH''') is the focus of the [[Construction]] skill. It can be bought from an [[estate agent]] for {{Coins|1000}}, or received for free upon completion of the [[miniquest]] [[Daddy's Home]]. Players' houses are located in [[Rimmington]] by default but can be moved to one of 8 different cities for a fee by talking to an [[estate agent]], if the required (unboostable) Construction level is met. Players can enter the house through [[Portal (Player-owned house)|house portals]], labelled on the [[world map]] as [[File:House portal icon.png]]. For a list of pros and cons on different locations consult the [[Portal (Player-owned house)|house portal]] page.

Additionally, owning a house is required for the following:
* Ability to use an [[experience lamp]] on the Construction skill<!--only tested this for [[lamp]] and [[Antique lamp (Client of Kourend)]], it is probably true for the level 30 and above requirement lamps as well-->
* Ability to gain Construction experience from repairing [[Wintertodt]] [[brazier]]s, [[Tempoross]] [[totem pole]]s, Tempoross [[Mast (Tempoross)|masts]] and [[Vale Totems|Vale Totem poles]]

